.TH GFAL-COPY 1 "" "gfal2-util 1.9.1" "xgfalclient"
.SH NAME
gfal\-copy \- copy a file or set of files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gfal\-copy
[\fIOPTION\fR]... [\fIsrc\fR] \fIdst\fR [\fIdst\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Gfal util COPY command. Copy a file or set of files.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.B src
source file
.TP
.B dst
destination file(s). If more than one is given, they will be chained copy: src \-> dst1, dst1\->dst2, ...
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
output version information and exit
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
enable the verbose mode, \-v for warning, \-vv for info, \-vvv for debug
.TP
.B \-D DEFINITION, \-\-definition DEFINITION
override a gfal parameter
.TP
.B \-t TIMEOUT, \-\-timeout TIMEOUT
maximum time for the operation to terminate \- default is 1800 seconds
.TP
.B \-E CERT, \-\-cert CERT
user certificate
.TP
.B \-\-key KEY
user private key
.TP
.B \-4
forces gfal2\-util to use IPv4 addresses only. N.B. this is valid only for gridftp
.TP
.B \-6
forces gfal2\-util to use IPv6 addresses only. N.B. this is valid only for gridftp
.TP
.B \-C CLIENT_INFO, \-\-client\-info CLIENT_INFO
provide custom client\-side information
.TP
.B \-\-log\-file LOG_FILE
write Gfal2 library logs to the given file location
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-force
if destination file(s) cannot be overwritten, delete it and try again
.TP
.B \-p, \-\-parent
if the destination directory does not exist, create it
.TP
.B \-n NBSTREAMS, \-\-nbstreams NBSTREAMS
specify the maximum number of parallel streams to use for the copy
.TP
.B \-\-tcp\-buffersize TCP_BUFFERSIZE
specify the TCP buffersize
.TP
.B \-s SRC_SPACETOKEN, \-\-src\-spacetoken SRC_SPACETOKEN
source spacetoken to use for the transfer
.TP
.B \-S DST_SPACETOKEN, \-\-dst\-spacetoken DST_SPACETOKEN
destination spacetoken to use for the transfer
.TP
.B \-T TRANSFER_TIMEOUT, \-\-transfer\-timeout TRANSFER_TIMEOUT
global timeout for the transfer operation
.TP
.B \-K CHECKSUM, \-\-checksum CHECKSUM
checksum algorithm to use, or algorithm:value
.TP
.B \-\-checksum\-mode {source,target,both}
checksum validation mode
.TP
.B \-\-from\-file FROM_FILE
read sources from a file
.TP
.B \-\-copy\-mode {pull,push,streamed}
copy mode. N.B. supported only for HTTP/DAV to HTTP/DAV transfers, if not specified the pull mode will be executed first with fallbacks to other modes in case of errors
.TP
.B \-\-just\-copy
just do the copy and skip any preparation (i.e. checksum, overwrite, etc.)
.TP
.B \-\-disable\-cleanup
disable the copy clean\-up happening when a transfer fails
.TP
.B \-\-no\-delegation
disable TPC with proxy delegation
.TP
.B \-\-evict
evict source file from disk buffer when the transfer is finished
.TP
.B \-\-scitag SCITAG
SciTag transfer flow identifier (number in [65\-65535] range) (available only for HTTP\-TPC)
.TP
.B \-r, \-\-recursive
copy directories recursively
.TP
.B \-\-abort\-on\-failure
abort the whole copy as soon as one failure is encountered
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
do not perform any action, just print what would be done
